@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+# Source correctness fixes
+
+Base revision: `1ab4f99a76adb530f86b278390ab8139ef41cc96`.
+
+## Runtime changes
+
+* Canal utility clamps the small-water-area penalty at zero with `max`, making
+  connections to a second water area larger than two tiles eligible for worker
+  evaluation. Existing ownership, city-work and adjacent-city guards remain.
+* Fort construction chooses the shortest legal base build time, retaining native
+  enumeration order for ties. The fort's canal/airbase location benefit is kept
+  separate from build choice. Distance scaling uses a wide intermediate and a
+  saturated result. This policy obtains the required access quickly; it does not
+  attempt to optimize defensive upgrades or total worker travel/build time.
+* `CvPlayerAI` save format 6 appends the agenda, score, update turn, bad-start
+  evidence, naval/logistics priorities, risk, expansion horizon, posture,
+  observed war state and all five agenda budgets. The reader retains its previous
+  defaults for versions 0–5. Disposable observation/path caches remain invalidated.
+* Python start/load handlers rebuild upgrade mappings once and replace both
+  arrays only after all lookups succeed. Repeated loads no longer append copies.
+* World Bank interest and Crusade spawning iterate actual owned cities through
+  `PyPlayer.getCityList`, including sparse native IDs. Their obsolescence guards
+  check `NO_TECH` before calling the native technology query.
+* Simultaneous-team rollover skips dead team slots and activates the first living
+  team. It stops searching only after a team has been activated.
+
+## Save and binary compatibility
+
+The source reader supports the older per-player AI formats through the existing
+version guards. Old saves cannot recover agenda history that was never recorded;
+they retain the documented default state until the usual update occurs.
+
+**Saves written by version 6 require an updated DLL. Older DLLs cannot consume the
+new extension safely.** Keep original saves when switching builds. The bundled
+DLL predates even the reviewed source and has not been replaced by these changes.
+Build the updated DLL and record its source revision and hash before engine tests.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run from the mod root with Python 3 and a C++03-capable `g++` with UBSan:
+
+```sh
+python3 Tools/test_review_correctness.py
+python3 Tools/run_regression_suite.py
+```
+
+Ten targeted tests execute actual native methods/fragments and Python handler
+bodies under narrow adapters. They cover canal guards, fort ordering/cost/score
+boundaries, all 16 live/dead arrangements of four team slots, save-extension field
+round trips and stream sentinels, agenda hysteresis after restoration, legacy
+extension defaults, repeated and failed mapping rebuilds, sparse city interest,
+obsolescence and Crusade spawning. Nine reject the original source; the obsolete
+bank control already passes. The new tests are registered in the full suite.
+
+The complete suite runs 15 isolated programs. Its former dead-document assertion
+now checks strategic budgets reaching city production; an unused civic-horizon
+XML define was removed without weakening the economic regression assertion. The
+existing serializer test now expects version 6 and retains its v4/v5 operation
+record tests. CRLF bytes are preserved in legacy runtime files.
+
+These checks do not build the complete Windows DLL or load a real BTS save.
+The stream adapter tests the appended extension and existing reset statements,
+not the full engine save container. Python handler tests run selected compatible
+bodies in Python 3, not the embedded Python 2 interpreter.
+
+The research prerequisite heuristic remains unchanged. Replacing recursive
+costs with a deduplicated AND/OR research-package search needs a separately
+specified algorithm and performance validation; a naive set union is insufficient.
